.TH UP 1 "2026" "eMerger 3.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
up \- eMerger, one-command system updater
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B up
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fB\-\-\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
This page covers \fBup\fR on Linux and macOS: every flag, environment and
configuration variable, file, exit status and JSON field. The plugin API and
the Windows build are in the eMerger manual, \fIdoc/documentation.pdf\fR.
.PP
eMerger detects the package managers installed on the host and runs each of
them in turn to refresh, upgrade and clean the system, then prints a summary.
It can also clean the user cache, the trash and, with \fB\-\-deep\-clean\fR,
system leftovers and unused container data. Every cleaning step asks first unless \fB\-y\fR is given.
.PP
Short flags from the set \fBh V n v q y w\fR can be bundled: \fB\-nv\fR is
\fB\-n \-v\fR. Other short flags (\fB\-nl\fR, \fB\-qq\fR, \fB\-up\fR and so on)
and long flags stay whole. A flag that takes a value accepts it as the next
word or as \fB\-\-flag=VALUE\fR (\fB\-\-only=apt,flatpak\fR); an empty value
exits 2. \fB\-\-\fR marks the end of options: the words after it are ignored.
.SH GENERAL
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show the help text.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print the version.
.TP
.B \-\-doctor
Run the environment health check. Exits non-zero if any check warns or fails.
.SH EXECUTION
.TP
.B \-n, \-\-dry\-run
Print the commands that would run, change nothing.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Stream package manager output instead of the live progress line.
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet, \-qq, \-qqq
Quieter output, one level per \fB\-q\fR or \fB\-\-quiet\fR. \fB\-q\fR hides
informational lines, \fB\-qq\fR prints only the one-line summary,
\fB\-qqq\fR prints nothing.
.TP
.B \-y, \-\-yes
Answer yes to every prompt.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the run summary as one JSON object on stdout, fields as in
\fBJSON OUTPUT\fR. Implies \fB\-nl \-ni \-qqq\fR. Warnings go to stderr.
.SH SELECTION
.TP
.B \-\-security
Security updates only, where the manager supports it (apt via
unattended-upgrade, dnf, yum, zypper, softwareupdate). Other managers are
skipped with a warning.
.TP
.B \-\-firmware
Include firmware: \fBfwupdmgr\fR, and on a Raspberry Pi with an EEPROM, stage
the bootloader update (\fBrpi\-eeprom\-update \-a\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-firmware
Skip firmware, including the Raspberry Pi bootloader check. Wins over
.B ARG_FIRMWARE=1
set in the config file or a profile.
.TP
.B \-\-dev
Include dev toolchains: rustup, cargo, npm, pnpm, pip, gem.
.TP
.B \-\-parallel
Run independent user-space managers at the same time.
.TP
.BI \-\-profile " NAME"
Load \fI~/.config/emerger/profiles.d/NAME.sh\fR, else the shipped
\fIshare/profiles/NAME.sh\fR of the checkout, before the command-line flags.
The last \fB\-\-profile\fR wins.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-profiles
List the available profiles.
.TP
.BI \-\-only " LIST"
Comma-separated managers to run (e.g. apt,flatpak).
.TP
.BI \-\-except " LIST"
Comma-separated managers to skip. Adds to a list set by the config or a
profile.
.SH SAFETY AND INTEGRATION
.TP
.B \-\-snapshot
Take a pre-update snapshot (snapper, timeshift or btrfs). Exit 1 before
any manager runs when none works.
.TP
.B \-\-rollback
Revert to the latest eMerger snapshot and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-refresh\-mirrors
Re-rank mirrors (reflector, netselect-apt) before upgrading.
.TP
.B \-\-resume
Skip managers that completed in the last run. A run without
\fB\-\-resume\fR starts a fresh cursor.
.TP
.B \-\-reboot
Reboot now if the system requires it.
.TP
.B \-\-reboot\-exit
Exit with status 4 instead of 0 when a reboot is required.
.TP
.B \-\-download\-only
Download packages without installing them (apt, dnf, pacman, zypper,
softwareupdate).
Every other manager is skipped with a message.
.TP
.B \-\-accept\-licenses
Let macOS
.B softwareupdate
accept licence agreements. Without it, it lists the available updates and
installs nothing.
.SH DISPLAY
.TP
.B \-nl, \-\-no\-logo
Hide the logo.
.TP
.B \-ni, \-\-no\-info
Hide the system information line.
.TP
.B \-w, \-\-weather
Show a weather line from wttr.in.
.TP
.B \-\-ascii
ASCII glyphs only. The spinner becomes the ".:" pulse.
.SH CLEANING
.TP
.B \-nc, \-\-keep\-cache
Skip user cache cleaning and the warning about space held by deleted files still open.
.TP
.B \-nt, \-\-keep\-trash
Skip trash cleaning.
.TP
.B \-\-deep\-clean
Also clean system leftovers, asking for each: journal above
\fBJOURNAL_MAX_SIZE\fR, old kernels (dnf, zypper), config files of removed
packages, disabled snap revisions, crash dumps, npm and Go caches. Then the
Containers section: stopped containers, unused images, build cache and
unused volumes of every local docker context (remote ones skipped) and of
podman (stopped containers and volumes never under \fB\-y\fR), and the size
of Docker Desktop's data.
.SH INSPECTION
.TP
.B \-\-changed
Show packages added, removed or upgraded in the last run.
.TP
.BI \-\-changelog " PKG"
Show the upstream changelog of \fIPKG\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-history
Show the last runs.
.TP
.BI \-\-metrics " FILE"
Export the last run as a Prometheus textfile with the gauges
\fBemerger_last_run_timestamp_seconds\fR,
\fBemerger_last_run_duration_seconds\fR, \fBemerger_last_run_errors\fR,
\fBemerger_last_run_freed_bytes\fR, \fBemerger_reboot_required\fR and one
\fBemerger_manager_ok\fR per manager.
.TP
.B \-err, \-\-errors
Show logged errors.
.SH MAINTENANCE
.TP
.B \-up, \-\-self\-update
Update eMerger with git (fast-forward only).
.TP
.B \-au, \-\-auto\-update
Install a weekly run (systemd user timer, or cron).
.TP
.B \-rc, \-\-rebuild\-cache
Clear the package manager detection cache.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Each variable below except the \fBXDG_*\fR ones can also be set in
\fI~/.config/emerger/config.sh\fR or a profile.
.TP
.B EMERGER_EMOJI
\fBauto\fR (default) uses emoji icons only when fontconfig reports a
color-emoji font; \fB1\fR or \fB0\fR forces the choice.
.TP
.B EMERGER_SPINNER
Spinner style: \fBbraille\fR, \fBdots\fR, \fBpulse\fR or \fBline\fR. Unset,
\fBbraille\fR on a UTF-8 terminal and \fBpulse\fR otherwise; without UTF-8
every style but \fBline\fR falls back to \fBpulse\fR.
.TP
.B EMERGER_PROMPT_TIMEOUT
Seconds a prompt waits before taking its default (60; 0 waits forever).
.TP
.B EMERGER_CACHE_TTL
Seconds the package manager detection cache stays valid (86400; 0 disables it).
.TP
.B DISK_MIN_FREE_MB
Warn and ask below this many MiB free on / (1024).
.TP
.B BATTERY_MIN_PCT
Warn and ask below this battery percentage (20).
.TP
.B RETRY_ATTEMPTS
Attempts for a step that fails with a transient network error (2, one retry).
.TP
.B RETRY_DELAY
Seconds before the first retry; the n-th retry waits n times as long (3).
.TP
.B CACHE_EXCLUDE
~/.cache entries never offered for cleaning (names or globs).
.TP
.B CACHE_MENU_ROWS
Cache entries listed before the rest is grouped as "others" (12).
.TP
.B JOURNAL_MAX_SIZE
Journal size \fB\-\-deep\-clean\fR vacuums down to (200M).
.TP
.B DEEP_CLEAN_SKIP
Deep-clean tasks to skip: journal, kernels, residual, snap, docker, podman,
coredumps, npm, go.
.TP
.B RPI_ABORT_ON_UNDERVOLTAGE
On a Raspberry Pi, abort even with \-y when the board is under-voltage (0).
.TP
.B RPI_TEMP_WARN
Raspberry Pi SoC temperature, in degrees C, at or above which to warn (80).
.TP
.B MANAGER_TIMEOUT
Seconds one manager command may run before \fBtimeout\fR stops it with
exit 124 (0, no limit).
.TP
.B DRY_RUN
1 previews every run, as \fB\-n\fR does (0).
.TP
.B UI_VERBOSE
1 streams manager output, as \fB\-v\fR does (0).
.TP
.B QUIET_HOURS
\fIHH:MM\-HH:MM\fR window, may wrap past midnight, in which a run with
\fB\-y\fR prints "quiet hours, skipping" and exits 0. A malformed value
warns and is ignored.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Any non-empty value disables colors.
.TP
.B COLORFGBG
\fIfg;bg\fR as set by the terminal: a background of 7 or more selects the
palette for light backgrounds.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME, XDG_CACHE_HOME, XDG_STATE_HOME
Base directories of the config, cache and state directories under
\fBFILES\fR (\fI~/.config\fR, \fI~/.cache\fR and \fI~/.local/state\fR when unset).
.PP
Numeric variables take whole numbers; any other value warns and the
default is used. The safety switches \fBDRY_RUN\fR and
\fBRPI_ABORT_ON_UNDERVOLTAGE\fR exit 2 on any other value instead.
\fBMANAGER_TIMEOUT\fR without a \fBtimeout\fR command warns once and is not applied.
.SH CONFIGURATION
\fIconfig.sh\fR and profiles can set the variable of each flag below, to 1
or to the flag's value. Command-line flags are applied after them and win.
A profile cannot select a profile. The flags that run an action or a query
instead of an update (\-h, \-V, \-\-doctor, \-\-list\-profiles,
\-\-rollback, \-\-reboot, \-\-changed, \-\-changelog, \-\-history,
\-\-metrics, \-err, \-up, \-au, \-rc) are taken from the command line
only: setting their variables in a file has no effect.
.PP
.nf
.ft CR
DRY_RUN              \-n
UI_VERBOSE           \-v
QUIET_LEVEL          \-q (0 to 3)
ARG_YES              \-y
ARG_JSON             \-\-json
ARG_SECURITY         \-\-security
ARG_FIRMWARE         \-\-firmware
ARG_NO_FIRMWARE      \-\-no\-firmware
ARG_DEV              \-\-dev
ARG_PARALLEL         \-\-parallel
ARG_ONLY             \-\-only LIST
ARG_EXCEPT           \-\-except LIST
ARG_SNAPSHOT         \-\-snapshot
ARG_REFRESH_MIRRORS  \-\-refresh\-mirrors
ARG_RESUME           \-\-resume
ARG_REBOOT_EXIT      \-\-reboot\-exit
ARG_DOWNLOAD_ONLY    \-\-download\-only
ARG_ACCEPT_LICENSES  \-\-accept\-licenses
ARG_NO_LOGO          \-nl
ARG_NO_INFO          \-ni
ARG_WEATHER          \-w
ARG_ASCII            \-\-ascii
ARG_KEEP_CACHE       \-nc
ARG_KEEP_TRASH       \-nt
ARG_DEEP_CLEAN       \-\-deep\-clean
.ft
.fi
.PP
\fB\-\-except\fR adds to \fBARG_EXCEPT\fR; every other flag replaces its
variable.
.SH JSON OUTPUT
\fB\-\-json\fR prints one object, and \fIhistory.jsonl\fR holds one per run:
.TP
.B ts
End time of the run, UTC, ISO 8601 (2026-01-31T09:00:00Z).
.TP
.B duration
Run time in seconds.
.TP
.B freed_kb
KiB freed by cache and trash cleaning.
.TP
.B errors
Number of managers that failed.
.TP
.B reboot
1 when a reboot is pending, else 0.
.TP
.B managers
One object per manager run: \fBname\fR, \fBresult\fR (\fBok\fR or \fBfail\fR)
and \fBsecs\fR, its run time in seconds.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/emerger/config.sh
Sourced before argument parsing. This file, user profiles, plugins and
hooks are refused unless you own them and no other user can write them.
.TP
.I ~/.config/emerger/profiles.d/*.sh
User profiles.
.TP
.I ~/.config/emerger/hooks/pre.d/*.sh, ~/.config/emerger/hooks/post.d/*.sh
User hook scripts, run in name order before and after the managers.
.TP
.I ~/.config/emerger/managers.d/*.sh
Manager plugins.
.TP
.I ~/.config/emerger/ignore.list
Packages pacman never upgrades, one per line; other managers get an advisory.
.TP
.I share/profiles/*.sh
Shipped profiles, in the eMerger checkout.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/emerger/detected
Detection cache, valid for \fBEMERGER_CACHE_TTL\fR seconds.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/emerger/emerger.log
Log file.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/emerger/history.jsonl
One JSON record per run.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/emerger/pkgs.before, pkgs.after, pkgs.diff
Installed packages before and after the last real run, and the difference
\fB\-\-changed\fR shows.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/emerger/resume
Managers that completed in the last run, read by \fB\-\-resume\fR.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/emerger/parallel-*.log
Output of each manager of a \fB\-\-parallel\fR run.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/emerger/emerger.lock
Global lock (\fBflock\fR; the directory \fIemerger.lock.d\fR without it).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Success.
.TP
1
Runtime failure (sudo, lock, disk, interrupted) or aborted (a declined
safety prompt, no snapshot taken with \fB\-\-snapshot\fR).
.TP
2
Argument parsing error.
.TP
3
One or more package managers failed.
.TP
4
Reboot required (only with \fB\-\-reboot\-exit\fR).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cron (8),
.BR systemd.timer (5)
